// The operator is a separate module so that controller-runtime, the Helm SDK
// and their transitive dependency trees never enter the driver's build. The
// driver ships in a container that mounts a node's block devices; every
// dependency it does not have is one that cannot be a vulnerability there.
//
// This workspace ties the two together for local development, so an edit to the
// driver's types is seen by the operator without a replace directive or a
// tagged release. CI builds each module on its own with GOWORK=off, because
// that is what `go install` and the release build actually do.
go 1.27.0

use (
	.
	./operator
)
